From 6e057e5811625814f0ff10b92601b966fc3bc3ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicole Muzzin <nicks@fuckin.email>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 03:03:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] properties: enable scroll-margin, scroll-padding,
 scroll-behavior and scroll-snap for Servo

These longhands and shorthands were Gecko-only, so Servo dropped them at parse
time and pages that use them (sticky-header sites relying on scroll-padding,
smooth-scrolling sites, snap carousels) got none of the behaviour. Servo's
script crate now implements scroll-into-view offsets, smooth scrolling and
mandatory snapping on top of them.

The scroll-snap-type and scroll-snap-align fields become public so script can
read the computed axis, strictness and alignment.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
